Feature: Migrate completed legacy execute checkpoints before identity enforcement
  As a developer upgrading a consumer repository
  I want fully completed and fully unbound legacy execute runtime released safely
  So that a different eligible queue can start with fresh identity on every supported OS

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Fully unbound terminal checkpoint starts a fresh queue
    Given issue 6 has a schema-version-1 checkpoint with every valid step complete
    And current, failure, remediation, and all six identity fields are absent or cleared as required
    When execute starts approved eligible issue 19
    Then only issue 6 run-owned runtime is released
    And issue 19 starts with a new complete native identity and revision
    And no checkpoint identity mismatch is emitted

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Partial identity and nonterminal legacy state remain blocked
    Given a checkpoint is incomplete, active, failed, remediating, malformed, or contains any identity-field subset
    When execute requests a different issue list
    Then it exits with exactly Run checkpoint identity mismatch
    And checkpoint bytes and supporting runtime are unchanged
    And no requested worker starts

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Legacy cleanup races and unsafe boundaries fail closed
    Given an otherwise eligible legacy checkpoint has a held lock, changed bytes, unsafe link boundary, deletion failure, or foreign controller ownership
    When execute attempts legacy cleanup
    Then no fresh run is created or advanced
    And cleanup does not escape the canonical runtime boundary or release foreign state

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Classification is invariant across serialized path forms
    Given deterministic fixtures combine LF and CRLF bytes with POSIX and Windows path-form identity values
    When eligible and partially identity-bearing shapes are classified
    Then every logical shape has the same migrate-or-reject result
    And fixtures use Node filesystem, path, process, and executable primitives only

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Native hosts preserve cleanup and identity safety
    Given the checkpoint-portability scenario runs natively on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows
    When legacy cleanup encounters each host's safe and unsafe filesystem boundaries
    Then exact owned runtime is removed only for eligible state
    And fresh project identity uses the native canonical root
    And locks, symlinks or junctions, stale revisions, branch or head drift, and foreign leases remain fail-closed
